 ## Background
-Acoustic Volume Rendering (AVR) is based on the work presented in "Acoustic Volume Rendering for Neural Impulse Response Fields" [S1]. It builds upon the Volume Rendering Integral [8682-volume-rendering-integral.md] and extends it to acoustic domains. The method is implemented in the AcoustiX platform, which is built on the Sionna ray tracing engine and supports reflection, scattering, and diffraction [S1]. Room models are created with Blender and exported in XML formats using the Mitsuba blender Add-on [S1].
